-- Rebuilds the `canvas:morning-briefing` workflow (id 0ad09fa0-…) from scratch.
--
-- The briefing that ran before 2026-07-29 fabricated most of its content: its
-- prompt interpolated the same merged `{{input}}` blob under four different
-- headings, and its system prompt told the model to "skip missing sections
-- silently" — so it filled the gaps with plausible invention (a sleep figure
-- when the health tool errored, an email count when Gmail's token had expired).
--
-- This graph makes that structurally impossible:
--   * every source is namespaced by its own `transform`, so provenance survives
--     the merge;
--   * `briefing-compose` renders pre-formatted, unit-correct facts plus an
--     explicit GAPS list and a source ledger recording what each signal did;
--   * `briefing-verify` checks every number, time and unit in the draft against
--     the facts the writer was shown, and replaces a draft that strays with a
--     plain rendering of the same facts.
--
-- 2026-10-03: the July version kept the model honest with prohibitions (quote
-- verbatim, never judge), which made it a flat readout. Judgement now lives in
-- code — baselines, rain hours, diary, email from people, yesterday's repeats,
-- the owner's votes — and the prompt asks for an editor's voice, because the
-- code check, not the prompt, is what stops fabrication. Calendar and news
-- joined as `site-tool` reads of Main's `apple_calendar_list` / `news_search`.
-- The writer continues on error: with no model, briefing-verify sends the plain
-- facts rather than the run stopping with no message at all.
-- Gmail now fetches headers so mail from people can be told from bulk mail
-- (with ids only, the old composer recorded Email as FAILED every morning).
--
-- Weather is fetched twice — at home, and wherever `person.john` actually is —
-- so the briefing reflects local conditions when he is away.
--
-- Node ids are uuid5-derived, so re-running this is idempotent.
-- Apply with:
--   docker exec -i strange-rambling-app-db-1 psql -U app -d strange_rambling < this-file
BEGIN;
DELETE FROM workflow_edges WHERE workflow_id = '0ad09fa0-5e17-40c2-9438-0604d6071a22';
DELETE FROM workflow_nodes WHERE workflow_id = '0ad09fa0-5e17-40c2-9438-0604d6071a22';
UPDATE workflows SET trigger = $SR${"type": "cron", "config": {"expression": "0 7 * * *"}}$SR$::jsonb, description = $SR$Verified-source morning briefing. Gathers location, weather at home and where John actually is, health, home sensors, email and knowledge-graph context; plus the diary and headlines; ranks what matters in code (baselines, rain hours, mail from people, yesterday's repeats, votes); has the LLM write it and checks every number against the facts; sends a WhatsApp summary and writes the full detail to /jkai/briefing.$SR$, updated_at = now() WHERE id = '0ad09fa0-5e17-40c2-9438-0604d6071a22';
COMMIT;
